      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s an odd asymmetry between this and ec_response_get_version version strings and EC_REBOOT_JUMP_RW.\n\nIn some cases, \"RW\" means \"RW-A\", and in some cases, it means \"Active RW image\", which could be RW-B.\n\nIt may be better to add a new command to get the active image, which more precisely handles *which* image (and maybe with space for a few flags).  That would also help the problem that we have to read 100 bytes of ec_response_get_version when 99% of the time all we care about is less than a byte of which image is active.",
